  },
  {
    "id": "dark-age",
    "type": "book",
    "title": "Dark Age",
    "creator": "Pierce Brown",
    "series": "Red Rising Saga",
    "seriesNumber": 5,
    "status": "finished",
    "rating": 5,
    "finished": "2026-06-29",
    "dateApprox": true,
    "added": "2026-06-29",
    "year": 2019,
    "pages": 704,
    "cover": "/shelf/dark-age.jpg",
    "color": "#e6c967",
    "review": "This book was amazing and filled with peaks. I think the weakness of expanding to multi POV was really felt by the last book, but this book thrives off it. \n\nOften left in suspense with a character, we go across the universe to another character in an equally perilous situation.\n\nFilled with action, amazing book. I hate Lysander, but he is a perfect villain for Darrow. In many ways, it seems pierce brown is trying to parallel Darrow with Lysander - an upstart from the death of a dear family member who is so dead set on a motivation.\n\nI’m not looking forward to more wins for Lysander, considering this book was full of losses for our side. Don’t know how Pierce Brown will write us out of this hole… or, if he even will? Is there really a happy ending to this story?",
    "link": "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/29226553"
  },
  {
    "id": "iron-gold",
    "type": "book",
    "title": "Iron Gold",
    "creator": "Pierce Brown",
    "series": "Red Rising Saga",
    "seriesNumber": 4,
    "status": "finished",
    "rating": 4,
    "finished": "2026-05-18",
    "dateApprox": true,
    "added": "2026-05-18",
    "year": 2018,
    "pages": 602,
    "cover": "/shelf/iron-gold.jpg",
    "color": "#fefdfd",
    "review": "I’ve seen harsh criticism of this book - but I really beg to differ.\n\nI think the main thing we lose here from the main series, is the pace. We’re introducing 4 different settings with completely new characters, so it takes some time to get going. And it’s clear this book is just setting up for more and more.\n\nLysander was by far the best POV of this book. Which is surprising, but Cassius and his duels - and Romulus’s death. Were so good \n\nDarrow was underwhelming.. but that was kind of the point? He had a whole book of basically missing the mark and building up his anger. \n\nEphraim was great, I was not a fan of Lyria",
    "link": "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/33257757"
  },
  {
    "id": "morning-star",
    "type": "book",
    "title": "Morning Star",
    "creator": "Pierce Brown",
    "series": "Red Rising Saga",
    "seriesNumber": 3,
    "status": "finished",
    "rating": 4,
    "finished": "2026-04-10",
    "dateApprox": true,
    "added": "2026-04-10",
    "year": 2016,
    "pages": 524,
    "cover": "/shelf/morning-star.jpg",
    "color": "#010217",
    "review": "The ending was fantastic.. everything that you’d want closed, was closed. \n\nI’m sad Victra was excluded from the final scenes, as she felt like a pivotal character throughout the book. \n\nThe cassius betrayal into double betrayal was so good. I do feel like the author gave us a little too many hints that something was going on, I caught on right before the reveal and I feel like that took a bit away.\n\nBut overall, really enjoyed this book and a perfect tie off to the trilogy",
    "link": "https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/18966806"
  },
