    "review": "Flawed, but great - juggling the 3 perspectives is difficult and makes it almost feel like a slog. But in isolation, the stories are great. The flaws come when combining them together and jumping between. \n\nThe continually increasing scope doesn’t feel daunting, it just always feels like there’s more to know. I hope the pay off is worth it for book 3",
